{"base_rate":0.46153846153846156,"brier":0.1912699564586357,"bss":0.2303661275831087,"bss_hi":0.32299606747711473,"bss_lo":0.13660610021915473,"chart":{"base":[660.5,169.5],"fp":[386.6,326.9],"lead":"62,186.3 272,164.5 482,136.1 692,49.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.23 — higher than 25% of cities","fp":"low end +16pp, high end +6pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.7 °C — better than 8% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 9%; promised 95% → rained 83%"},"rel":"62,427 77.3,386.7 161.8,283 422.4,138.1 660.4,108.6"},"country":"CA","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.16731494920174167,"ess":430.502762367684,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Quebec</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Quebec rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 8 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>90%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>9%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 689 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-29. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSAINTE-FOY 1.8 ENE, 6.4 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.23, ranked 101 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(63&ndash;116) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>122</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>20%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>17%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>9%</td><td class='num'><b>34%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'><b>51%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'><b>73%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>68%</td><td class='num'><b>79%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>90%</td><td class='num'><b>76%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>90%</b></td><td class='num'>69</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">8 of 9 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Quebec</b> <span class=\"muted\">CA</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">8 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.23</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>63&ndash;116\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>689 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Quebec &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" ro