ircle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"91.25605633802817\" cy=\"258.9577464788732\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 22%&amp;#10;It rained 51% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"136.26794520547944\" cy=\"197.50684931506848\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 45%&amp;#10;It rained 73% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"218.99074626865672\" cy=\"115.7910447761194\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 68%&amp;#10;It rained 79% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"300.2877142857143\" cy=\"96.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 90%&amp;#10;It rained 76% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"377.5608571428571\" cy=\"106.40000000000003\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 90% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 69 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.1791304347827\" cy=\"54.92753623188406\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(46%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Quebec the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.38) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.06).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>165</td><td class='num'>52%</td><td class='num'>-0.059</td><td class='num'>25.2%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>159</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>0.177</td><td class='num'>12.4%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>193</td><td class='num'>49%</td><td class='num'>0.373</td><td class='num'>13.4%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>172</td><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'>0.378</td><td class='num'>11.8%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":46.81228,"lon":-71.21454,"n":689,"n_cities":134,"name":"Quebec","offset_days":-1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.01,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":122,"obs":0.09016393442622951,"sig":true},{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.01,"mean":0.014024390243902441,"n":82,"obs":0.1951219512195122,"sig":true},{"hi":0.06,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.03707692307692308,"n":65,"obs":0.16923076923076924,"sig":true},{"hi":0.15,"lo":0.06,"mean":0.09394366197183099,"n":71,"obs":0.3380281690140845,"sig":true},{"hi":0.3380000000000007,"lo":0.15,"mean":0.22109589041095887,"n":73,"obs":0.5068493150684932,"sig":true},{"hi":0.58,"lo":0.3380000000000007,"mean":0.4547761194029851,"n":67,"obs":0.7313432835820896,"sig":true},{"hi":0.81,"lo":0.58,"mean":0.6844285714285714,"n":70,"obs":0.7857142857142857,"sig":false},{"hi":0.9720000000000004,"lo":0.81,"mean":0.9027142857142857,"n":70,"obs":0.75714285